        "duration_ms": 54673,
        "node_output": "## 1. Scope\n\n### Includes\n- Advancing `projectkoios-bootstrap` from a scaffolded three-harness repo into an **operational feature-planning builder**.\n- Standardizing **Pi as the default Archon assistant** across Archon-facing docs and workflow definitions.\n- Making the **handoff boundaries explicit** between:\n  - `archon/` = architecture, planning, ADRs\n  - `opencode/` = implementation, tests, validation\n  - `goose/` = vault/knowledge/ingestion/UI-bootstrap support\n- Adding or refining workflow/docs/templates in this repo only:\n  - `archon/workflows/`\n  - `archon/prompts/`\n  - `architecture/`\n  - `README.md`\n  - optionally harness-boundary docs/rules in `opencode/` and `goose/`\n\n### Excludes\n- No Python/package code in component repos such as `projectkoios-agent`, `projectkoios-api`, etc.\n- No changes to `maps/packages.md` or `maps/repositories.md` unless repo/package ownership actually changes.\n- No implementation of feature code in sibling repos.\n- No vault-note generation in `../projectkoios-notes/` unless explicitly requested later.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Approach\n\nUse `projectkoios-bootstrap` as intended by `architecture/adr.20260628.md`: a **meta-harness** with strict harness separation.\n\nThe next phase should make Archon’s “plan feature” flow produce a more actionable output by:\n1. using **Pi** as the default assistant for Archon work,\n2. collecting repo/ADR context,\n3. producing a structured plan with explicit repo/file ownership,\n4. routing follow-on work to the correct harness instead of letting Archon absorb implementation or knowledge tasks.\n\nThis should also correct current drift:\n- `.archon/config.yaml` says `assistant: pi`\n- `archon/workflows/*.yaml` still use `provider: codex`\n- `architecture/adr.20260629.codex-for-archon-workflows.md` is now stale relative to the new Pi default\n- `README.md` still describes older Archon install guidance\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation steps\n\n| # | Step | Files / repos | Harness |\n|---|------|---------------|---------|\n| 1 | Document the Pi switch as an architecture decision. Add a new ADR superseding `architecture/adr.20260629.codex-for-archon-workflows.md`, or revise ADR history if you prefer an amendment model. | `architecture/adr.<date>.pi-for-archon-workflows.md` or update existing ADR set in `projectkoios-bootstrap` | **archon** |\n| 2 | Update Archon workflow definitions to align with Pi and make planning output more structured. Replace `provider: codex` with Pi-compatible config and add explicit sections for scope, repo ownership, dependencies, open questions, and harness routing. | `archon/workflows/plan-feature.yaml`, `archon/workflows/design-review.yaml`, `archon/workflows/create-adr.yaml` | **archon** |\n| 3 | Add reusable prompt assets instead of embedding all behavior in YAML. Create prompts for feature planning, ADR drafting, and harness-routing guidance. | `archon/prompts/plan-feature.md`, `archon/prompts/create-adr.md`, `archon/prompts/harness-routing.md` | **archon** |\n| 4 | Add an explicit harness-boundary reference doc so workflow outputs can cite one operational source of truth in addition to ADR20260628. | `architecture/harness-boundaries.md` or `maps/harnesses.md` in `projectkoios-bootstrap` | **archon** |\n| 5 | Tighten README and bootstrap instructions so operator behavior matches the new default. Update Archon setup, Pi default assistant notes, and clarify when to use each harness. | `README.md`, possibly `AGENTS.md` | **archon** |\n| 6 | Add an opencode-side handoff contract describing what a plan from Archon must contain before implementation begins. | `opencode/rules/specification_gate.md`, optionally new `opencode/rules/handoff.md` | **opencode** |\n| 7 | Add a Goose-side handoff contract for when planning work requires vault research, note curation, or source-ingestion prep rather than code implementation. | `goose/AGENT.md`, optionally new `goose/prompts/research-support.md` | **goose** |\n| 8 | Validate cross-file consistency after edits: Pi default, harness boundaries, install/setup docs, and workflow usage examples all agree. | `projectkoios-bootstrap` repo-wide review | **opencode** |\n| 9 | Optionally create one acceptance artifact: run the updated `archon/workflows/plan-feature.yaml` against a sample feature and save the output as an example for future operators. | `examples/` if added, or `architecture/` example note in `projectkoios-bootstrap` | **archon** |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Dependencies\n\n- Archon must support the intended **Pi assistant/provider configuration** model.\n  - Current state is mixed: `.archon/config.yaml` uses `assistant: pi`, workflows use `provider: codex`.\n- Decision on ADR policy:\n  - supersede old assistant ADR, or\n  - amend/replace it in place.\n- Agreement on whether harness-boundary guidance belongs in:\n  - `architecture/` as durable design documentation, or\n  - `maps/` as operator-facing canonical routing.\n- Optional but useful: a standard format for Archon-to-opencode work orders.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Open questions\n\n1. **How should Pi be declared in Archon workflows?**  \n   Is `provider: pi` correct, or should workflows omit `provider` and rely on `.archon/config.yaml`?\n\n2. **Should the Codex ADR be superseded or edited?**  \n   The cleaner history is likely a new ADR that explicitly supersedes `architecture/adr.20260629.codex-for-archon-workflows.md`.\n\n3. **Do we want a formal handoff artifact?**  \n   Example: a markdown work-order template that Archon emits and opencode consumes.\n\n4. **Should Goose be invoked only on explicit research/vault tasks, or also as a default pre-planning context collector for notes?**\n\n5. **Do we want examples/tests for workflows?**  \n   If Archon workflow testing is lightweight, a sample planned feature artifact would help keep prompts stable.\n\n6. **Should README install guidance be updated to match `architecture/adr.20260629.md` exactly?**  \n   Current README still shows older curl-install wording.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Harness assignment\n\n### Archon owns\n- ADRs and durable architecture/planning docs\n- workflow YAMLs\n- prompt templates\n- harness-boundary definition\n- sample feature-plan generation\n\n### opencode owns\n- implementation-facing rules\n- validation that docs/workflows/rules are internally consistent\n- future code changes in sibling repos once a plan is approved\n\n### Goose owns\n- knowledge/vault/research support prompts\n- any optional note-sync or curation flows\n- ingestion/search/UI-bootstrap knowledge tasks, not core planning orchestration\n\n## Recommended sequencing\n\n1. **archon** — new Pi ADR  \n2. **archon** — update workflow YAMLs  \n3. **archon** — add prompt files + boundary doc  \n4. **archon** — update README/usage docs  \n5. **opencode** — add implementation handoff/spec gate updates  \n6. **goose** — add research-support handoff guidance  \n7. **opencode** — consistency review  \n8. **archon** — run one sample plan as acceptance proof\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a ready-to-save ADR or a task checklist file for `projectkoios-bootstrap`.",
